{
 "name": "memo_redisclosure_cases",
 "version": 3,
 "rule": "F13 memo re-disclosure (Paul approved 2026-09-26, \"Approve F13\"). A memo row whose own text states that it re-discloses a gift already itemized (receipt role unverified_disclosure_memo: a memo matching fec_receipt_rules.json disclosure_pattern) is a duplicate of the counted parent it restates - same company, same recipient committee, same contributor (contributor_id when both rows carry one, else the normalised name), the same nonzero amount to the cent, dated on or before the memo, not itself a memo - and counts once, via the parent (reason memo_redisclosure_of_counted_parent, parent sub_id recorded). Several parents: the latest-dated, then the lowest sub_id. The filer's own statement is the proof (lane J3, 2026-09-26, restoring the approved rule after lane J2 had required the same day). A memo that calls the gift unitemized restates no itemized parent. With no parent the memo stays counted and flagged disclosure_memo_unmatched (D-040). A memo without the statement is untouched. A counted parent: company match accepted or blank, no excluded_reason, a giving role.",
 "format": {
  "defaults": "merged under every row",
  "rows": "receipt rows as the Mentat tables hold them (memo_code X / is_memo_leg 1 marks a memo)",
  "expect": "sub_id -> {counted: stays in the total, duplicate_of: parent sub_id or \"\", flagged: counted re-disclosure memo carrying disclosure_memo_unmatched}",
  "statements": "receipt_type_full / memo_text -> states (a re-disclosure statement) and unitemized, for the shared patterns; real phrases name the saved industry they come from"
 },
 "defaults": {
  "company": "Coinbase",
  "committee_id": "C00835959",
  "filing_form": "F3X",
  "company_match_status": "accepted",
  "excluded_reason": ""
 },
